# Lighthouse — web runtime credentials.
#
# Copy to `web/.env.local` and fill in. Next.js loads `.env.local` automatically; no
# library and no import are needed. That file is gitignored (`web/.gitignore` has `.env*`,
# which is also why this template has no leading dot — `.env.example` would be ignored
# too, and a template nobody can see is not a template).
#
# Nothing here is required to run the app. `npm run dev` works with this file absent:
# the safety gate, the crisis banner, and the chat all function, and the UI states that
# replies are scripted. That is the "if the API is down, triage still works" property
# from CLAUDE.md, exercised as the default path rather than as an untested branch.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — optional. Turns scripted replies into real ones.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used ONLY to write the assistant's chat replies (`src/lib/intake.ts`). It never sees a
# tier, never proposes one, and its output is never read by the classifier. If you are
# looking at this variable while trying to change how a tier is decided, you are in the
# wrong file — that is the Python side.
#
# NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. That would ship your key to every student's browser.
#
# Before setting this on a deployment, read `docs/improvements.md` §1. `/api/chat` needs
# no auth and there is no rate limiting, so the code-side bounds are all there is: a turn
# is truncated at MAX_TURN_CHARS, a request is refused past MAX_CONVERSATION_TURNS, a call
# is capped at INTAKE_MAX_TOKENS and retried INTAKE_MAX_RETRIES times. Those bound one
# request, not one hour of them. Set a spend limit in the Anthropic Console — it is the
# only control that holds regardless of what the code does — and mint a fresh key for the
# deployment rather than reusing this one, so it can be revoked without breaking local dev.
#
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL — needed to persist anything at all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon serverless Postgres. Create the tables with `npm run db:push`.
#
# Without it the app falls back to an in-memory store and says so, loudly, in the console
# and in the override panel. That fallback is for local work only: on serverless each
# instance has its own memory, so a counsellor's override can be written by one instance
# and be invisible to the next — a correction silently disappearing rather than a stale
# cache. Counsellor accounts, the audit log, break-glass and retention all need this set.
#
# Free tier at https://neon.tech — create a project, copy the pooled connection string.
# Format: postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIGHTHOUSE_CLASSIFIER_URL — optional, and the one that fails silently
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The HF Space serving the turn classifier. Live chat calls it with a timeout and degrades
# to gate-only triage on failure (CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS in src/lib/config.ts).
# Seeded demo data ships with precomputed scores, so the demo never depends on it.
#
# Read by `classifierUrl()` in src/lib/classifier.ts and called from /api/chat. Unset is a
# normal deployment, not a misconfiguration: `scoreConversation` returns `not_configured`,
# the gate-only card already written is kept, and both the queue and the case page say
# "gate only". Nothing logs an error, because nothing went wrong. That is also why a
# deployment that MEANT to have a classifier can sit there scoring nothing and look fine.
#
# Locally this is http://127.0.0.1:8000 with `uvicorn lighthouse.serve.app:app` running
# (docs/deploy.md §3b). Never copy that value to Vercel: there it resolves to the
# serverless function itself. Deploying the Space is docs/deploy.md §4.
LIGHTHOUSE_CLASSIFIER_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIGHTHOUSE_PII_KEY — required once anything is stored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AES-256-GCM key for the PII map: the only place a student's real names, places and
# contact details exist, and they are sealed with this before they touch the database.
#
# A database dump without this key yields redacted transcripts and nothing else. That is
# the entire point — so in a real deployment it lives in a secret store, NOT beside
# DATABASE_URL, because holding both is equivalent to holding plaintext.
#
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# Rotating it makes every existing sealed span permanently unreadable. There is no
# recovery path and that is deliberate.
LIGHTHOUSE_PII_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRON_SECRET — required before the retention job will run at all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guards `/api/retention`, which erases conversations past their retention date. Sent as
# `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET`; Vercel Cron does this for you.
#
# Unset means the route refuses both verbs with a 503 rather than running unauthenticated.
# An open endpoint that deletes children's disclosures is worse than a retention job that
# has not been configured yet, and the second failure is visible where the first is not.
#
# The verb is not the safety mechanism, the explicit `apply` is. Vercel Cron can only
# issue GET, so `vercel.json` schedules `/api/retention?apply=1` and that query parameter
# is load-bearing: without it the same GET is a dry run that reports what would go.
#
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
CRON_SECRET=
